Later that day I continued with the Budget App project.
I added the logic, what percantages where withdrawn from the ledger. I created a for-loop to go over each item in the spent_amounts list.
In that loop I initialzed a few attributes, which store the different mathematical applications, such as dividing each item through the total number of items
and multiplying it with 100. 
Then rounding that number to the nearest 10th with math.floor and then multiplying it with 10. The result is stored in the percentanges list.
